  "description": "What a value of one of OpenStreetMap's numeric tags, which OpenStreetMap writes as text, becomes, wherever Curio loads it: a length (keys.lengths) in metres, a unit converted (m, metre, metres, meter, meters, km, mi, nmi and ft in any case, and feet and inches); a speed (keys.speeds) in km/h, km/h, mph and knots converted; a count (keys.counts) from a plain number alone; null for any other text. A plain number, written as the expression language writes one, stays the number it writes, as does one written in its key's own unit; a value converted from another unit is rounded to two decimals as JavaScript's Math.round rounds. A number stays the number it is, and any other key is handed on as it came. Both twins run these cases: withOsmNumbers in autkDataCompile.ts, which both of an Autark node's loaders hand their tables on through, the sandbox's code (compileDataSpecToAutkDbJs, which embeds its source) and the browser's (loadSpecLayers), and its Python twin, osm_values.py in the backend's discovery/domain, which the Discovery Catalog's OpenStreetMap downloads write their numbers with. The values from the shipped extracts are marked with their extract.",
